# Gmail API Credentials Hook

# This hook provides Gmail API credentials via injection
# The credentials are never stored in plain text in the vault
# Instead, they are securely injected at runtime

# The following environment variables should be available when this hook is used:
# GMAIL_CLIENT_ID - Your Gmail API client ID
# GMAIL_CLIENT_SECRET - Your Gmail API client secret
# GMAIL_ACCESS_TOKEN - OAuth2 access token
# GMAIL_REFRESH_TOKEN - OAuth2 refresh token
# GMAIL_USER_EMAIL - The email address to monitor

# Instructions for setting up Gmail API credentials:
# 1. Go to Google Cloud Console: https://console.cloud.google.com/
# 2. Create a new project or select existing one
# 3. Enable Gmail API for the project
# 4. Create OAuth2 credentials (Desktop application)
# 5. Download the credentials JSON file
# 6. Set up OAuth2 flow to get access and refresh tokens
# 7. Store tokens securely in your system (not in this file)

# This hook file is a placeholder - actual credentials should be
# injected via your secure credential management system.
# The skill will access these via environment variables or other secure means.